DTSTART:20261003T190000Z
DTEND:20261003T210000Z
SUMMARY:Simchat Torah Learning and Celebration with Rav Jonathan 10/3/26, 5:45 pm at Anshe Emet Synagogue
DESCRIPTION:Simchat Torah is the festive celebration of the completion and renewal of the Torah reading cycle. We're excited to celebrate with you! Hosted by Rav Jonathan, we will gather at Anshe Emet Synagogue for some learning and orientation to the holiday and its traditions. Then, we will join the rest of the community for a service followed by singing and dancing with the Torah! \n\nOrganizer: Metro Chicago Hillel\nRSVP Link: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScW505Lx-_ru-ai3rzbFI9elOFZqDfod1KO6F9DYMxXfBZeKQ/viewform
LOCATION:Metro Chicago Hillel
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScW505Lx-_ru-ai3rzbFI9elOFZqDfod1KO6F9DYMxXfBZeKQ/viewform
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cmusx5ydr0057123s8wewgh77@jewishevents.chi
DTSTAMP:20261003T220219Z
DTSTART:20261003T220000Z
DTEND:20261004T020000Z
SUMMARY:Mishkan Chicago Brings Back: Simchat Torah!! (aka Mishkan's Big Torah Party)
DESCRIPTION:Simchat Torah is the last of the torrent of fall holidays: the crown, the top, the end, the last gasp, the finale– and is all about celebration of how far we&#8217;ve come, and where we&#8217;re going next. Join Rachel Mylan and Rabbi Ari Moffic at 5:00 PM to kick off the night with a celebration for kids and families with bite-sized amounts of Torah reading, dancing and singing, followed by a community pizza party. Our grown-up celebration with Rabbis Lizzi, Steven, Julie, and the Davening Team, starts at 7:00 PM with singing, circles of dancing, Torah reading and Mishkanites sharing their own hot Torah takes as we celebrate Jewish wisdom in all its forms. Register\n\nOrganizer: Mishkan Chicago\nRSVP Link: https://www.mishkanchicago.org/event/simchat-torah-10-03-26/
LOCATION:CJDS, 3730 N California Ave, Chicago, IL, Chicago
URL:https://www.mishkanchicago.org/event/simchat-torah-10-03-26/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
