SUMMARY:Saturday Morning Unplugged
DESCRIPTION:The things you love about Mishkan in the morning: music, stretching, learning, and inspiration. We&#8217;ll be recognizing and celebrating new builders at this service! Programming Saturday Morning Mishnah Study at 8:45 am: Our study session with Rabbi Steven diving into Pirkei Avot returns Rise &amp; Shine at 10:00 am : Stories and songs for kids ages 0-4, with guest instructor Esther Fishbein! Mah Tovu: Art at 11:00 am: Artistic projects and a children’s service for grades K-5. Registration required &nbsp; There will not be ASL provided for this service. Watch the livestream on the Mishkan YouTube channel. Coming for the first time? Let us know who you are so we can give you a special hello and introduce you to other Mishkanites. Looking to help out? We’re in need of volunteer greeters to welcome people into Mishkan before services. You can sign up here or email Michael at michael@mishkanchicago.org for more information\n\nOrganizer: Mishkan Chicago\nRSVP Link: https://www.mishkanchicago.org/event/saturday-morning-unplugged-10-24-2026/
